CM 1MHz_tower's all-copies-loaded twin (momwire#415): the same geometry with
CM one LD per leg, written out.  The symmetry is retired by GX 0 0 -- a GX
CM selecting no plane, which nec2c's reflc treats as a cell reset and which
CM adds no wire -- so the wire list is bitwise the as-written deck's and only
CM the addressing changes.  Writing the GR out as 100 GW cards would be the
CM other way to say this, and would not be bitwise: a rotation's coordinates
CM cannot be spelled on a card.  momwire's answer here must equal its answer
CM for 1MHz_tower.deck exactly.
